From: Cast contributors <cast@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] input: convert presentation-only timestamps before stream output

An FLV can begin with video DTS before the container's start time. The
avformat demuxer then supplies invalid/nonpositive DTS but valid PTS.
DecoderFixTs only converts timestamps when its primary timestamp is valid.
Passing DTS as primary left the first PTS in stream time while subsequent
packets used system time. The TS muxer's DTS=PTS fallback exposed this as
a large discontinuity, corrupting HLS duration and HTTP relay startup.

Convert a valid PTS independently in that case. Keep DTS invalid for the
existing downstream fallback and preserve both the valid-DTS path and the
both-invalid path. Do not invent, clamp, or shift source timestamps.

--- a/src/input/decoder.c
+++ b/src/input/decoder.c
@@ -846,8 +846,17 @@ static int DecoderPlaySout( decoder_t *p_dec, block_t *p_sout_block )
     }
 
     DecoderWaitUnblock( p_dec );
-    DecoderFixTs( p_dec, &p_sout_block->i_dts, &p_sout_block->i_pts,
-                  &p_sout_block->i_length, NULL, INT64_MAX );
+    if( p_sout_block->i_dts <= VLC_TICK_INVALID &&
+        p_sout_block->i_pts > VLC_TICK_INVALID )
+    {
+        /* Cast modification, 2026-09-09: keep presentation-only packets on
+         * the system clock. Muxers may derive DTS from the converted PTS. */
+        DecoderFixTs( p_dec, &p_sout_block->i_pts, NULL,
+                      &p_sout_block->i_length, NULL, INT64_MAX );
+    }
+    else
+        DecoderFixTs( p_dec, &p_sout_block->i_dts, &p_sout_block->i_pts,
+                      &p_sout_block->i_length, NULL, INT64_MAX );
 
     vlc_mutex_unlock( &p_owner->lock );
 
